---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Gallery from '../components/Gallery.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../components/QuoteForm.astro';
import { projectsIn } from '../lib/media';
import { serviceSchema, breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const path = '/hialeah-pergolas/';
const title = 'Pergolas Hialeah FL | Patio Covers for Small Yards';
const description =
  'Pergolas and patio covers in Hialeah — attached structures sized for compact lots, driveway and carport covers, and getting real usable shade out of a small backyard.';

const crumbs = [{ href: '/service-areas/', label: 'Service Areas' }, { label: 'Hialeah' }];

const schema = [
  serviceSchema({
    name: 'Pergola and patio cover installation in Hialeah, Florida',
    description,
    path,
    serviceType: 'Pergola construction',
    areaServed: ['Hialeah, Florida', 'Miami-Dade County, Florida'],
    offers: ['Attached patio covers', 'Compact custom pergolas', 'Driveway and carport covers', 'Aluminum pergolas'],
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, path),
  webPageSchema({ path, name: title, description }),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path={path} crumbs={crumbs} schema={schema}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Hialeah"
    title="Pergolas in Hialeah: Getting Real Shade Out of a Small Yard"
    lede="Hialeah backyards are compact, hard-working and usually bounded by a wall or a fence on every side. That is not a limitation on what you can build — it is a design brief. When there is no room for error, proportions and post positions matter far more than they do on a big open lot, and a well-fitted structure transforms the space in a way an oversized one never will."
    facts={[
      { label: 'Typical lot', value: 'Compact, walled or fenced, often with limited side access' },
      { label: 'Typical build', value: 'Attached patio covers and slim freestanding structures' },
      { label: 'Design driver', value: 'Maximum usable shade from minimum footprint' },
      { label: 'Also common', value: 'Driveway, carport and entryway covers' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Small yards reward custom work more, not less</h2>
      <p>
        There is a common assumption that a custom structure is something you do on a big
        property and a stock-sized cover is what you settle for on a small one. In practice
        it is the other way round.
      </p>
      <p>
        On a large lot, a structure that is a foot too deep or has a post six inches off is
        barely noticeable. On a Hialeah backyard, that same error is the difference between a
        space you can walk around comfortably and one where you turn sideways to get past the
        table. Post positions, beam overhang and headroom all have to be right, and a stock
        size cannot give you that by definition.
      </p>
      <p>
        The good news is that small structures are the least expensive kind of custom work.
        Shorter spans mean lighter members, smaller footings and a faster build. Custom here
        is not the premium option; it is the sensible one.
      </p>

      <h2>Attached is usually the answer</h2>
      <p>
        In a compact yard, every post you plant is floor area you lose. An attached structure
        — one that ties into the house and extends the roof line outward — puts only two posts
        in the yard instead of four, which on a small deck is a substantial difference in how
        the space feels and how furniture can be arranged.
      </p>
      <p>
        The detail that matters is the tie-in. It has to carry load into something that can
        take it, and it has to shed water away from the wall rather than into the junction.
        On the flat-roofed and tile-roofed houses common across Hialeah, both are entirely
        solvable — they just need doing properly rather than quickly. More on this on the{' '}
        <a href="/pergolas/installation/">pergola installation page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Walls, sun and privacy</h2>
      <p>
        A yard enclosed by masonry walls holds heat, and the walls themselves bounce sun back
        into the space in the afternoon. A solid or insulated roof helps considerably more
        than an open rafter roof does in this situation, because it stops the direct load
        rather than just filtering it — and it gives you a ceiling for a fan, which in an
        enclosed yard makes a real difference.
      </p>
      <p>
        Privacy usually comes free with the walls, but overlooking from a neighbouring second
        storey is common. A slat screen on one side of the structure resolves it without
        closing the space in, and it doubles as protection against low western sun.
      </p>

      <h2>Driveways, carports and entryways</h2>
      <p>
        Not every structure in Hialeah goes in the backyard. Covers over a driveway parking
        area, a carport extension, or a shaded entryway are all common requests, and they are
        built the same way as any other structure — set-out, footings, frame, roof. The
        constraints are different (vehicle headroom, setbacks, visibility from the street)
        but the principles are identical.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/pergolas/aluminum/">Aluminium</a> is almost always the material here: it
        holds a clean line, needs no refinishing, and looks right against the rendered and
        painted masonry that dominates the neighbourhood.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-sand">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our work</p>
        <h2>Compact structures, properly proportioned</h2>
      </div>
      <Gallery projects={projectsIn('pergolas')} limit={2} />
      <p style="margin-top:var(--space-l)">
        <a class="btn btn-dark" href="/gallery/">See every project</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell form-band">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Get a pergola quote in Hialeah</h2>
        <p>
          Photograph the yard from the back door and from the far corner, and give us the
          rough dimensions of the space including the wall or fence lines. Mention the width
          of the side gate — on a compact lot that decides how the structure gets staged.
        </p>
        <p>
          Also see <a href="/miami-pergolas/">Miami</a>,{' '}
          <a href="/kendall-pergolas/">Kendall</a> and the full{' '}
          <a href="/service-areas/">service areas list</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <QuoteForm service="Pergola" city="Hialeah" compact />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="A small yard is a solvable problem."
    body="Send photographs and dimensions and you will get an honest read on what fits — including when the right structure is smaller than you were picturing."
    secondaryLabel="Pergola options"
    secondaryHref="/pergolas/"
  />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .form-band { display: grid; gap: var(--space-l); }
  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .form-band { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); gap: var(--space-2xl); align-items: start; }
  }
</style>
